							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1377.msg13727#msg13727"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1377.msg13727#msg13727">Re: Still Play?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #5 on:</b> January 17, 2005, 08:28:47 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							The rumors of Everquest&#039;s demise have been greatly exxagerated.<br /><br />For every guild that&#039;s folded, FoT or Hegemony or Ruination, there&#039;s another guild like League of Sozoban or Dawning Nemesis or Inner Loop that have grown and thrived in the last few months.&nbsp; Server merge would be a nightmare.&nbsp; We&#039;re fine with who we have.&nbsp; And yea, I expect EQ to steal successful ideas from other games - that&#039;s how mmorgs work.&nbsp; Aren&#039;t we getting in-game mail with the next expansion?&nbsp; 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
